#
# --- area 3, DINING ROOM -- found in live play 2026-09-03 --------------------
# The player called it before any tool did: "there isn't a door at (18,19). There
# is furniture in area 3 -- the door you have detected is probably the furniture
# just on the north side of the wall in (18,20)." Confirmed off a 5x grid-
# annotated page render. The module text says "a number of tables and chairs",
# and the map draws TWO LONG TABLES with stools ranged around them, several of
# them hard against the room's south wall.
#
# (18,19,H) measured thick=17 -- squarely in B1's WALL band (7-18) and nowhere
# near its DOOR band (4-11). The classic signature, and the seventh fabricated
# door found in this map. The wall runs unbroken; the stools sit wholly on the
# room side, which is the one test that separates furniture from a door.
edge	18	19	H	wall	dl+claude	area 3: stools/table drawn against the SOUTH wall, read as a door (thick=17, hole=44). No opening here at all.
edge	18	20	H	open	dl+claude	area 3: interior grid line between the two tables, read as a door (thick=12, hole=75)
edge	19	20	H	open	dl+claude	area 3: interior grid line, read as a door (thick=4, hole=74 -- 4 is the printed-ruling band)
#
# --- area 2, KITCHEN -- found in live play 2026-09-03, player again ----------
# THE THICKNESS TEST DID NOT CATCH THIS ONE. (13,20,H) measured thick=9, which is
# INSIDE B1's genuine door band (4-11), and confidence 9. What gave it away was
# the player knowing area 2 is a furnished kitchen. At 10x zoom the wall between
# rows 20 and 21 is thick, solid and unbroken across the full width, and a long
# COUNTER is drawn hard against its south face inside the kitchen, leaving a thin
# white gap above the furniture line. That gap is the "hole=200".
#
# LESSON: an in-band thickness does NOT clear a door that opens off a furnished
# room. Furnished rooms in B1 so far: 2, 3, 9, 18, 24, 27, 28.
edge	13	20	H	wall	dl+claude	area 2 KITCHEN: counter drawn against the north wall, read as a door (thick=9 IN BAND, hole=200). Wall is unbroken at 10x.
